Problem statement
Versions are numbered 1 through n. Starting at one unknown bad version, every subsequent
version is bad. The judge provides isBadVersion(version). Find the first bad version while
minimizing calls to that function.
Input & expected result
The displayed bad value defines the judge's hidden behavior; it is not an argument to your search
function.
EXAMPLE 1
Input: n = 8, bad = 6
Output: 6
Explanation: Versions 1 through 5 pass; versions 6 through 8 fail.
EXAMPLE 2
Input: n = 1, bad = 1
Output: 1
Explanation: The only version is the first bad version.
Constraints & guarantees
• 1 <= bad <= n <= 2^31 - 1
